<section class="mb-5">
  <div class="card shadow-sm border-0">
    <div class="card-body p-4 p-lg-5">
      <h2 class="h1 mb-3">Sand Point Way can be better</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Sand Point Way NE runs through northeast Seattle, connecting the University
        District to Magnuson Park and beyond to Lake City. For decades it was designated
        as State Route 513, prioritizing motor vehicle movement.
      </p>
      <p class="mb-4">
        The highway designation has been truncated to Magnuson Park, but the road culture has not caught up north of the park.
        <strong>Beyond SR 513</strong> is a community advocacy effort pushing for
        safer crossings and pedestrian-friendly streetscaping
        along Sand Point Way NE.
      </p>
      <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/get-involved/">Get involved</a>
        <a class="btn btn-outline-primary" href="/about/">Learn more</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="row g-4 mb-5">
  <div class="col-md-6">
    <div class="card h-100 shadow-sm">
      <div class="card-body">
        <h2 class="h4 card-title">The problem</h2>
        <p class="card-text">
          Sand Point Way NE has long stretches with no safe crossings, narrow or
          non-existent sidewalks, and fast-moving traffic that makes walking or
          moving on wheels feel dangerous.
        </p>
        <p class="card-text mb-0">
          Nearby destinations should be better connected: Magnuson Park with its fields, beach, open area, and arena; the Burke-Gilman Trail; and residential
          neighborhoods.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="col-md-6">
    <div class="card h-100 shadow-sm">
      <div class="card-body">
        <h2 class="h4 card-title">Why now</h2>
        <p class="card-text mb-0">
          We believe a road that once moved state highway traffic can be redesigned
          to move people on foot, on wheels, and in transit while
          remaining an arterial for cars.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mb-5">
  <h2 class="h3 mb-3">Our vision</h2>
  <div class="list-group shadow-sm">
    <div class="list-group-item">Protected pedestrian crossings at every major intersection</div>
    <div class="list-group-item">Continuous sidewalks on both sides of the road</div>
    <div class="list-group-item">A marked crossing connecting the Burke-Gilman Trail to Magnuson Park</div>
    <div class="list-group-item">Purposeful bus stops for Metro Route 75</div>
  </div>
</section>

